    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d389">

                <pb facs="0530" n="522" sameAs="frus:frus1941v04/pg522"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/2377a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-10-17T22:00:00-05:00">October 17,
                            1941—10 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>674. For the Ambassador and the Counselor only. Mr. Wakasugi talked on October 16
                    with the Secretary and the Under Secretary but no new points were developed. Mr.
                    Wakasugi is to call again on the Secretary and the Under Secretary on October
                        17.<anchor n="35" xml:id="d389-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d389-f1" n="35" xml:id="d389-f1-content">
                <p>See memorandum by the Secretary of State, October 16 and 17, 1941, <ref
                        target="frus1931-41v02#pg_687">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, Japan, 1931–1941, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, p. 687</ref>.</p>
            </note>
